            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">
              Is a treadmill over $2,500 actually worth it for most home users?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              For most casual walkers and occasional joggers, no. The jump
              in this tier mainly benefits frequent runners logging
              significant weekly mileage, buyers who specifically want
              extreme incline training, or households where multiple
              people put heavy, sustained wear on the machine. If you run
              under 10-15 miles a week and don't need incline training
